  "text": "Planning Document: docs/dcps/INNERWEST/Marrickville/Marrickville DCP 2011 - 9 10 Dulwich Hill North.pdf\n\nClause 9.10.2 - heritage (development_control): To protect and preserve the identified period buildings within the precinct and \nencourage their sympathetic alteration or restoration.\n\nClause 9.10.2 - heritage (development_control): To protect the identified Heritage Items  within  the precinct.\n\nClause 9.10.2 - height_limit (development_control): To maintain distinctly single storey streetscapes that exist within the precinct.\n\nClause 9.10.2 - heritage (development_control): To protect groups or runs of buildings which retain their original built form \nincluding roof forms, o riginal detailing and finishes.\n\nClause 9.10.2 - heritage (development_control): To protect  significant str eetscapes  and/or public domain elements within the \nprecinct including landscaping, fencing, open space, sandstone kerbing and \nguttering, views and vistas and prevailing subdivision patterns.\n\nClause 9.10.2 - zoning (land_use_zoning): To preserve the predominantly low density residential character o f the pr ecinct.\n\nClause 9.10.2 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): To ensure that new  development considers all potential impacts to biodiversity.\n\nClause 9.10.2 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): To ensure that n ew development  respects local fauna by minimising lighting \nimpacts on nocturnal fauna; reinforcing the permeability of the GreenWay Corridor \nto the surrounding built environment for local fauna; and providing a minimum 3 \nmetre native vegetation buffer between the GreenWay C orridor and any new \ndevelopment.\n\n",
